{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery to make an investigation and study of a  certain current Senate documents relative to the mental health of children in schools.","BillNumber":"S2789","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J18","Name":"Joint Committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J18","ResponseDate":"2024-05-15T16:05:27.543"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2789/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, May 20, 2024 -- The committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1273) of John C. Velis, Mark C. Montigny, James K. Hawkins, Patrick M. O'Connor and other members of the General Court for legislation relative to the mental health of children in schools, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2789).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate document numbered 1273 relative to the mental health of children in schools.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J18","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J18"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}